  "report_sha256": "a9133c94e01789bb80298de290f17177f71ae428f6d827142bd287722dca9793",
  "scope": "Two reversed-order repetitions compare restart versus retention across two consecutive 32-admission batches, with initial checking included in the two-worker mean. All eight workers and their intermediate catalogs replay without fresh recognition or reference search. Per-batch operations, admissions, maintained catalogs, scheduling, closure, next selections and delta hashes agree. All 3830 reference nodes are independently checked; all 3803 previous payloads and 1220 artifacts across 25 prior manifests are unchanged. Coverage stays 66/83. Eleven interrupted parent entries and thirteen interrupted first-batch entries are reentered, charged and stored; seven final entries remain unstored. Exact reuse includes nineteen prior-batch nodes, an empty-CNF terminal and an empty-clause refutation. The true 32-variable cofactor remains structurally pending despite a checked SAT witness. Retention requires exclusive ownership of immutable old rows/caches and checked maintenance. Cold reconstruction, copying, digests, exports and guard costs remain charged. No peak-RAM, persistent-space reduction, new Lean theorem, holdout or unrestricted-SAT efficiency claim. Tests and the initial LaTeX build ran concurrently with the start of cold validation, after the matched producer had finished; the final LaTeX build followed cold validation. The profiled startup sample includes profiler overhead and is not a speed comparison.",
